      },
      {
        "text": "Government entails power, force, and the ability to prohibit actions or seize property and freedoms.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Force, power, and violence are significant concepts in political discourse.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Violence involves physical action.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The phrase 'government is just another word for things we choose to do together' is analytically vacuous.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Barney Frank made statements reflecting the view that government is equivalent to collective choices.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "In some academic institutions, mild offense or challenges to existing worldviews are labeled as violence.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "Politics today are currently confusing.",
