    "episode_id": 84776,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/4/84776.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 101,
    "turn_text": "I want to argue with you or not so much argue or talk with you just a little bit about a general theme of your recent speech. You said in effect that the politicians, the elected officials have really let the people down. They've been disappointing. The people aren't getting their money's worth and so on. And I suppose there's some truth to that. But I often think, and I'm sure you agree to an extent, that in a democracy like ours, people get what they deserve or what they ask for. or vote for. And yes, the politicians are responsible, but so are people. And I often say that if you don't like what you call the mess in Washington, what one calls the mess in Washington, look in the mirror. All these people were sent there by voters, I think most of our, I'm rather pro politician. And it's odd for me to take a pro politician line with a politician. uh... but i think the people often get off scott free when we assigned blame",
