    "turn_text": "Yeah, I'm basically in your camp on this. When you listen to national media and to the politically obsessed, everything is Tea Party versus establishment or leadership versus outsiders. I, over the course of the 16 months of my campaign, again, I have 14-year-old girl, 11-year-old girl, four-year-old boy, we lived on a bus and we traveled to Nebraska's 93 counties tirelessly and got to know everybody in our state Real people don't really care about that. They really care about the direction of the country. And they don't really like student council race, personality centric reporting on politics. They're really disengaged from that. And again, to your earlier point about looking in the mirror, to a certain level, that's a problem. There's a crisis of engagement. But at another level, there is a Washington obsessed crowd that really doesn't understand coffee shops across America. And most of that establishment versus outsiders, establishment versus based stuff doesn't connect with real people. And I'm kind of happy that most real people aren't paying attention to that.",
